use @piton/belay

export instruction CommentLanguage:
    description:
        Write all code comments in ASD-STE100 Simplified Technical English.
        This applies to each comment and each doc comment in all code, in
        Rust, TypeScript and every other language.

    rules:
        - Write sentences of 20 words or fewer.
        - Use approved words. Use one word for one meaning.
        - Write technical names as they are.
        - Put one topic in each sentence.
        - Use the active voice.
        - Use the simple present, simple past or simple future tense.
        - Do not use -ing forms, contractions or phrasal verbs.
        - Use articles. Write noun clusters of 3 words or fewer.

    existingComments:
        The rule applies to each comment that exists now, not only to the
        comments that you add or change. When you find a comment that does not
        obey the rule, write it again in ASD-STE100.
